Package: zenith-printer
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://git.mixlake.com/yanjilu/zenith-printer
Description: LAN label design and printing service
 A single-process service that designs labels in the browser and prints them
 on NIIMBOT (serial) and Honeywell (ZPL over TCP 9100) hardware. It carries
 its own web interface, its own SQLite database and its own fonts, and needs
 no reverse proxy.
 .
 The fonts are bundled deliberately rather than taken from the system: the
 renderer runs with system font loading disabled so that one template prints
 identically on every machine. The exact bytes are pinned by a checksum
 manifest and verified when this package is built.
 .
 There is no authentication. Anyone who can reach the port can print and can
 cancel other people's jobs, so the service belongs on a LAN or a VPN and
 nowhere else.
